A||N||18||NOS3800||NOS users pleeze HELP!||||9||
Z||000000||NOS3800||11-12-2001||06:47 PM||||OK, went to the track with Lildv1L and Jason H(don't know his PFF screen name)this weekend. We had a horrible time. More on that in another post. My problem is this.<BR>I replaced my platinum plugs with cheapy Champion 103's cause I was told they run colder. Also, I have been using Octane Booster the past three times at the track. OK, my problems. On my runs, there is a powerloss at mid track, like a surging. Comes and goes while on the run.The first two times I stopped the run, the next two times I continued the runs with ET's much slower then usual. The fourth run was the same but the ENgine Service Light started flashing telling me of a bad misfire, so I let off. I pulled the plugs closest to the trunk and they looked fine. When I got home I changed the Champions out for the AC Delco Platinums. I found that the plug to the left against the fire wall had the ground electrode burned off! That explains the misfire, but why did it burn off? I don't think its lean cause the other plugs look fine. Could it have been gapped wrong? So I did two more runs on Sunday, I also decreased the NOS and increased the fuel, but still got the same problem. <BR>Here is my theory on this. I have been leaving my NOS bottle in the trunk over nite for the last three weeks(half full). I had the bottle refilled this weekend, but only needed it filled half way. Could the NOS be bad? I have made runs with these jets about 5 other times with no problems. These problems started when I changed the plugs and started to leave the bottle outside with the temps dropping to 40 degrees at nite. Need help. Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||9
