Z||000014||Shaun41178||11-14-2001||01:43 PM||||I wouldn't jump out and empty your bottle just yet.  When you did your test for 13 seconds did the nitrous come out foggy the whole time?  If so then it was all nitrous and most likely the rest is good too.<P>Just a tip here:  When you go to have your bottle filled freeze it first.  This will lower the pressure in the bottle so when they go to fill it they won't need to use the pump as much so you will get more nitrous and less air into your bottle.  By your bottle being frozen the higher pressure from the filling bottle will flow nice and easy into your low pressure bottle.<P>Thats good that you seem to have found the problem with the misfire.  When you get the new box back let us know if the problem has gone away.  And don't rush to get rid of your Zex kit.  You seem to be doing good with it.  If the problem happens again then I would go with Travis and get a NX kit.  If it keeps happening then it could do even more damage then just a burnt plug.<P>Plugs gapped at .053 seem to be ok since you havent' had any misfires previously.<P>I never ever used octane booster.  In fact I think NOS recommended not to use them when using nitrous and to use higher octane fuel only.  At least I am pretty sure I read that  in my owners manual for my nos kit.  Plus I don't think octane boosters did anything anyways.  They don't add that much.  You can get better results by adding toulene.  1 gallon of toulene to 10 gallons 93 Octane will net you about 101 octane.  However since the Fiero tank is only 10 gallons I would add like half a gallon toulene and race with half a tank of fuel to keep weight down.  If the booster hasn't been working for you then don't buy it anymore.  Waste of money I think.  I always used 92 or 93 octane and had my timing set straight up.||||reg||1
Z||000015||jimmybpei||11-14-2001||04:42 PM||||Travis- Have not put the kit on the car yet the heads are at the machine shop now , almost done.<P>Do you have any pictures discribing the location of the nozzel, as well would like to see the intake tube. I am using the cold intake setup from the fiero store with the dual over the roof snorkels and a HOLLEY side scoop, so i should be gettin lots of air<P>The motor: 30 over, froged flattop pistions <BR>arp bolt felpro cooper ring head gaskets heads planned  20  roller tip rockers small block chevy springs 148 196 (i think) valves with a 3 angle job headers 47? cam (thats wit the rockers) getting t- body and plenim from darryl not sure on which ignition system (msd or crane) have headers and thats about it i think all feed to the power losin auto tranny.<P>Have been taking notes on what you've been running for jets and their hp, as well as your 1/4 mile time. <P>Should be interesting on here next summer.<P>THanks for the info<P>Later <BR>Jimmy B.||||reg||1
Z||000016||NOS3800||11-14-2001||06:25 PM||||Thanks for the compliments MR2KLR. I remember that show in the pic, horrible weather.  Go to my website for some newer pics and the new interior at <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/bills3800" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/bills3800</A> <BR>The side scoops were mad eby me, and they were a pain in the butt. Took me forever to get the driver side done, thats why there was only one on the car at the show.<BR>Yeah, I am hoping the bad box will solve the problem. I am not ready to give up on the ZEX kit just yet, it has been great all  summer, I was even getting ready to break 1FST2M6's record before these problems started. Got down to a 13.21 with tire spin through 60 foot. I fattened the NOS jet and couldn't stop spinning. I would let off then get back in it and it would spin again. Managed 13.3's still though. But alas, I am done for the season cause the track is closed. May get a final chance in Dec. when I do the HPP magazine Shootout.<BR>||||reg||1
